## Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Vite + React project.

### Changes Made:

1. **Installed Package**: Added `@vercel/speed-insights` to project dependencies
   - Installed using npm (project's package manager)
   - Package version added to package.json
   - Lock file (package-lock.json) updated

2. **Modified Files**:
   - `src/App.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights component
     - Imported `SpeedInsights` from `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
     - Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the BrowserRouter, after the Routes component
     - This placement ensures Speed Insights tracks all route changes and page navigation

3. **Build Verification**:
   - ✓ Build completed successfully with no errors
   - ✓ All assets generated properly
   - ✓ No linting issues (no linter configured in project)
   - ✓ Build time: 642ms

### Implementation Details:

Following the official Vercel Speed Insights documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), I used the React-specific implementation:

- Used the React-specific export path: `@vercel/speed-insights/react`
- Placed the component at the app root level within BrowserRouter for comprehensive tracking
- No additional configuration needed - Speed Insights will automatically start collecting metrics

### Next Steps:

Once deployed to Vercel, Speed Insights metrics will be available in the Vercel dashboard under the Speed Insights section. The component will automatically collect and report Core Web Vitals and other performance metrics.

### Files Changed:
- package.json (dependency added)
- package-lock.json (lockfile updated)
- src/App.tsx (SpeedInsights component added)
